## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public Netlify
  `frontend-next/` beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- Migration numbering is authoritative: Phase 11 = admitted AI extensions,
  Phase 12 = Club/Community, Phase 13 = Cutover.
- Price Intelligence 1A shipped through PR #74. Feature head
  `1b7f93e10bcb859a5e5cd5c0a3384494fa964c99` was squash-merged as
  `f2469958a855ebfc6e37f99bdc292f6c423bb1a8`; the PR contains nine task files
  and excludes `.wslconfig`, which is pre-existing local work.
- Price Intelligence 1A consists of the migration
  `20260824120000_price_intelligence_1a_observations.sql`, a read-only service
  contract/adapter and deterministic adapter tests. It adds no UI, no smart
  price in `/vendi`, no external provider and no paid API.
- `public.wine_price_observations` is append-only and stores integer cents plus
  snapshots of `wine_id` and `formato`. ASKING observations are written only on
  real activation or an active price change; reservation release
  `riservato -> attivo`, same-price changes and metadata-only changes write
  nothing. SALE is written when an order first reaches `completato`; the partial
  unique index on `origine_ref` prevents a second SALE after
  `completato -> contestato -> completato`.
- The public `security_invoker = off` view `public.wine_price_history` exposes
  exactly 11 closed columns and excludes `origine_ref` and personal/domain
  identifiers. `anon` and `authenticated` can SELECT the view but have no base
  table privilege. The base table has RLS enabled and zero client policies.
- Three privileged writer/trigger functions are `SECURITY DEFINER`, have an
  empty `search_path` and no client/service-role EXECUTE ACL. UPDATE, DELETE and
  TRUNCATE are also rejected by append-only triggers even for `service_role`.
- The SQL grid ran on disposable PostgreSQL 17.10 from bootstrap `9c` through
  all 36 migrations: final result **32 PASSA / 0 FALLISCE**, zero fixture
  residue, never production. Cases 31-32 prove the real post-completion dispute
  route does not duplicate SALE.
- Full `frontend-next` verification was green: lint 0 errors / 14 pre-existing
  warnings, typecheck clean, **681 pass / 0 fail** across 46 files and 17,238
  expectation calls, production build green and `git diff --check` clean.
  `MIN_TESTS` is 681 in CI and the prelaunch regression contract.
- PR #74 and post-merge CI run `32734863290` were green for frontend,
  frontend-next and backend. The merge commit's Supabase Preview check was also
  green.
- Production project ref was verified as `pijnmcllmfgjmgsvtcej`. The pre-merge
  PostgREST baseline had 9 active public listings while both new objects were
  absent (404). The post-merge Supabase integration applied only migration
  `20260824120000`; the live ledger now ends at that version.
- Production backfill is **9 ASKING / 0 SALE** for 9 active listings. All nine
  ASKING rows match current `listings.prezzo_cents`; none was imported from
  `prezzo_mercato_cents`. Every row has truthful acquisition timestamp
  `2026-08-24 13:49:02.895298+00`, 35.895298 seconds after the merge timestamp.
- Production catalogs confirm the expected table, enums, five enabled domain
  and append-only triggers, CHECK constraints, unique partial SALE index,
  zero policies, closed 11-column view, RLS and role privilege matrix.
  Rollback-wrapped SQL proofs rejected anon/authenticated INSERT and rejected
  service-role UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE; row count remained 9.
- Anonymous PostgREST SELECT/POST/PATCH/DELETE on the base table all fail with
  HTTP 401 / PostgreSQL `42501`; anonymous view SELECT succeeds and reports 9
  rows. Authenticated PostgREST was **NON VERIFICATO** because no existing
  authenticated JWT was available and no account/fixture was created.
- No external price provider exists: no key, HTTP call, cron, adapter or flag.
  Activation stays fail-closed and would require a new migration and explicit
  provider/budget authorization.
- Price Intelligence 1B shipped from branch `feat/price-intelligence-1b-insights`
  off `main` at `e47a9e96258fc8970261021b3272890be8dfb761`. Pre-existing
  untracked `.wslconfig` was left out of the commit and remains local work.
- 1B adds no migration and no remote write. It reads `public.wine_price_history`
  through the existing 1A adapter and reuses the active listings that
  `/annuncio/[id]` already loads for its related-wines block; the only new
  database read is the price history itself.
- The 1A read contract gained one alternative key: `storico` accepts
  `wineSlug` instead of `wineId` (mutually exclusive in the type). `Wine` was
  not widened to carry `wine_id`. Both columns are already exposed by the view,
  so neither branch touches the base table.
- 1B analytics live in `frontend-next/src/lib/price-intelligence/insights.ts` as
  pure deterministic functions: comparables, median, range, coverage band, last
  observed change, chart series and time domain. Nothing there reads the clock,
  the network or input order.
- Reference rule: comparables are active listings with the same wine slug and
  the exact same format, deduplicated by listing identity. Under 3 comparables
  no number is produced at all. At 3 or more the reference is the **median** of
  asking prices, never the arithmetic mean, with min→max range and the
  comparable count shown.
- ASKING and SALE are never merged. Sales are counted and plotted; they do not
  move the 1B reference. Last observed change uses only the two most recent
  ASKING observations and is labelled "ultima variazione rilevata", not a trend.
- Coverage bands are 0-2 "In formazione", 3-4 "Bassa", 5-9 "Media", 10+ "Alta",
  presented as data coverage and not as accuracy or statistical guarantee.
- The panel always shows source "Dati interni Vinea", the analysed format, the
  ASKING/SALE observation counts and the active comparable count. A failed
  history read degrades to "Storico prezzi non disponibile" while the rest of
  the listing page and the comparable-based reference keep working.
- `/annuncio/[id]` no longer renders the legacy struck-through `prezzoMercato`
  next to the asking price. The DB column, the `ListingService` mapping, the
  `Wine` field and `WineCard` are untouched: only that one reading surface was
  removed.
- Smart Sell Price is live in the `/vendi` price step. The hard-coded
  `260 / 300 / 120` producer placeholder is gone from the panel and from the
  price-field placeholder; no other numeric fallback replaced it.
- `frontend-next/src/lib/price-intelligence/smart-sell-price.ts` defines no
  algorithm. It composes the existing 1B primitives `comparabiliAttivi`,
  `riferimentoRichieste` and `copertura`. Threshold, median, exact-format rule,
  listing-identity dedup and coverage band exist in exactly one place.
- Comparables are the active public listings in `public_listings` for the same
  wine key and the same exact format. Under 3 comparables no number is produced;
  at 3 or more the panel shows the 1B median, the min→max range, the comparable
  count and the coverage band, always sourced as "Dati interni Vinea".
- SALE observations have no input path: `smartSellPrice` takes no observations
  parameter, so sale history cannot move the suggestion.
- The suggestion never writes the price field. Only "Usa questo prezzo" applies
  it, and it applies the median exactly. The manual field stays usable in the
  loading, insufficient-data and failed-read states.
- `richiedeConfermaPrezzoPrecedente` separates "prefilled" from "chosen": an
  untouched inherited price still requires confirmation, while typing a price or
  applying the suggestion counts as an explicit choice and skips it.
- `ListingService` gained `elencoConEsito()` over the same query as `elenco()`.
  A failed read is distinct from an empty list, so a PostgREST error no longer
  reads as "no comparables"; `elenco()` stays tolerant for the catalog pages and
  the provider error detail stays internal.
- The Smart Sell Price read is keyed by `[wineKey, formato]`, so a response for
  the previous bottle cannot survive a bottle change or overwrite the current
  one, and loading, insufficient-data and error remain three distinct states.

